/*
 * sync-to generator — core.entity_view_display.bb_run.bb_run.teaser
 *
 * ONE RUN AS ONE ROW — the item of the Run history zone in the ticket detail's
 * body. BB-336 made `teaser` the row and `full` the run detail overlay, and
 * BB-414 ships the row because `core.entity_view_display.bb_ticket.bb_ticket.full`
 * renders the ticket's `runs` reference in this mode.
 *
 * IT NAMES THE SAME COMPONENT AS ITS ENTITY MAPPING, and that is a checked
 * statement rather than a convention: `data-display-components.sh` check B7 reads the addresses out
 * of `entity-mapping/bb_run.bb_run.teaser.jsonata` and out of this whole file
 * — comments included, in BOTH address forms — and fails when the two sets
 * differ. The mapping composes the row from exactly one container, so this
 * generator names exactly that one.
 *
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * `items` IS BOUND TO A SOURCE THIS PROJECT SHIPS, and the previous revision of
 * this header — which declared the row's cells inexpressible and bound nothing —
 * was right about the registry and wrong about the conclusion. Both halves are
 * kept, because the measurement is what makes the binding legible.
 *
 * The container owns its items. Its one content-bearing prop is `items`: an
 * ARRAY of items whose `cells` are keyed maps over eight declared kinds.
 * display_builder's prop bindings are `{source_id, source}` pairs, and
 * `SourcePluginManager::filterDefinitionsByPropType()` offers a source only when
 * the source declares the prop's PropType. ui_patterns' compatibility checker
 * guesses `items` as the `unknown` PropType — it does not descend into an array
 * item's object `properties` — and NO contrib source declares `unknown`: zero of
 * the 819 definitions on a provisioned site, measured rather than assumed. The
 * consequence was not a prop that got dropped but a prop that could not be
 * addressed, and `list.twig`'s `{% if items is not empty %}` rendered NOTHING —
 * three runs, three components of 91 bytes, all of them SDC comments.
 *
 * What was missing was a source, and a source is code this project can ship.
 * `bb_core`'s `BbRunRowSource` (plugin id `bb_run_row`) declares
 * `prop_types: ['unknown']` and a required `entity:bb_run` context, and
 * returns the ONE item this run is — the same shape, cell for cell, that
 * `entity-mapping/bb_run.bb_run.teaser.jsonata` composes, glyph map
 * included. So the row is DATA built in PHP, exactly as the inspector's rail is
 * (`Drupal\bb_core\Ticket\TicketInspectorRows` states the rule: `items` is a
 * prop, props carry scalar data only, a cell is data). The difference is only
 * who holds it — a screen's rail belongs to a controller, a run's row belongs to
 * the run's own view mode, and a view mode reaches PHP through a source.
 *
 * WHAT STAYS TRUE: no CONTRIB source can express this, so the binding names a
 * bakers plugin and the `dependencies.module` list is unchanged — `bb_core` was
 * already there. The source's own kernel test pins the `unknown` guess, so a
 * ui_patterns release that starts guessing a real PropType for an array of
 * objects is a red test rather than a silently empty zone.
 *
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * `dependencies` IS THE FIRST-SAVE FORM and the `uuid` is pinned — BB-414 R2,
 * for the reason the page-layout generator writes out in full: the recipe's
 * strict list compares this file against ACTIVE config on every construction,
 * ignoring only `uuid`, `_core` and an empty `dependencies`, so a twice-saved
 * form aborts the whole recipe on the second `ddev init`, and a `config/sync`
 * copy without a `uuid` makes `drush cim` manufacture exactly that second save.
 */
